To get the GNSS timestamp on Android, follow these steps:

1. First, you need to add the necessary permissions to your AndroidManifest.xml file. Add the following line:
```xml
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />
```
2. Next, import the necessary libraries in your Java or Kotlin code. For example:
```java
import android.location.Location;
import android.location.LocationListener;
import android.location.LocationManager;
import android.os.Bundle;
import android.widget.TextView;
```
3. Create a class that implements the LocationListener interface. This class will handle the location updates. For example:
```java
public class GNSSListener implements LocationListener {
    private TextView textView;
    private LocationManager locationManager;

    public GNSSListener(TextView textView) {
        this.textView = textView;
        this.locationManager = (LocationManager) getSystemService(Context.LOCATION_SERVICE);
    }

    @Override
    public void onLocationChanged(Location location) {
        // Get the current timestamp
        long timestamp = location.getTime();
        // Display the timestamp on the TextView
        textView.setText("GNSS timestamp: " + timestamp);
    }

    @Override
    public void onStatusChanged(String provider, int status, Bundle extras) {}

    @Override
    public void onProviderEnabled(String provider) {}

    @Override
    public void onProviderDisabled(String provider) {}
}
```
4. Finally, create an instance of the GNSSListener class and set it as the LocationListener for the LocationManager. For example:
```java
TextView textView = findViewById(R.id.textView);
GNSSListener listener = new GNSSListener(textView);
locationManager.requestLocationUpdates(LocationManager.GPS_PROVIDER, 0, 0, listener);
```
This will start receiving location updates from the GPS provider, and the timestamp will be displayed on the TextView.

